nsistently  across the world now so this is the  first step g7 agreement we've got to  move to the g20 and then beyond  but obviously the intention would be  once there is a global multilateral  solution in place then the need for  those dsts falls away  and how do you square a global minimum  corporate tax rate with  the importance of tax sovereignty i mean  aren't you potentially tying your own  hands if you have this minimum rate  in future well i think what the british  public want to know is that the tax  system is fair they want to know that  there is a level playing field so  whether people are operating in tax  havens  or whether large particularly online  businesses are able to  not pay tax in the right places they  want that tackled and that's what this  agreement  gives us the ability to do and it's been  agreed  amongst g7 colleagues and once we've  broadened it out and implement it  globally it's a huge prize for british  taxpayers it's slightly  slightly less ambitious than the  original proposal that global minimum  not 21  but 15 does that undermine you know the  strength of this agreement some people  suggest it does  well i'd say a couple of things first of  all what the agreement reached here  today says at least  15 and secondly it's worth taking a step  back this is something that's been  talked about for  almost a decade and here for the first  time today we actually have  agreement on the tangible principles of  what these reforms should look like  and that's huge huge progress final  question if i may the prime minister  said just uh recently that he'd been  looking at the data and he saw no reason  why uh there shouldn't be a change to  that plan june the 21st for  ending lockdown you obviously look at  the data an awful lot as well i just  wonder what your senses  of what that data's saying at the moment  with regard to lockdown well no final  decisions have been made we're looking  at the data as it as it comes in and as  the prime minister said  you know we need to make sure that we  vaccinated  and protected enough people to give us a  reassurance we need  given the new variant that is currently  in the uk  and it's too early to say where that  will conclude but as the data comes in  we're looking at it and a decision will  be made  as we've communicated in advance of june  21st okay
 

